# Copy to .env and fill in your credentials.
# NEVER commit .env — it is listed in .gitignore.
# These are required for local Maven Central publishing + GPG signing.
#
# CI (publish.yml) passes all credentials as environment variables,
# not -P flags — the PGP key block (SIGNING_KEY) is multi-line and
# breaks shell command line expansion.
#
# To generate a key pair locally:
#   gpg --full-generate-key
#   gpg --list-keys --keyid-format LONG     # copy the key ID
#   gpg --export-secret-keys --armor <KEY_ID>   # for SIGNING_KEY
MAVEN_CENTRAL_USERNAME=
MAVEN_CENTRAL_PASSWORD=
# Note: MAVEN_CENTRAL_USERNAME/PASSWORD must be a Central Portal User Token
# (generated at https://central.sonatype.com/), NOT a legacy OSSRH token.
# Legacy OSSRH credentials return HTTP 401 at the Central Portal OSSRH
# Staging API endpoint.
# SIGNING_KEY_ID is no longer consumed by the build -- the signing plugin
# extracts the key ID from the PGP private key block automatically.
# Kept here for backwards compatibility; can be safely removed.
SIGNING_KEY_ID=
SIGNING_KEY=
SIGNING_KEY_PASSWORD=
# ---
# Artifact coordinates:
#   ch.trancee.meshlink:meshlink-crypto        (main metadata, for Gradle consumers)
#   ch.trancee.meshlink:meshlink-crypto-android (Maven consumers)
#   ch.trancee.meshlink:meshlink-crypto-jvm     (Maven consumers)
#   ch.trancee.meshlink:meshlink-crypto-ios     (Maven consumers)
